  "reason": "A restored snapshot is not a durable effect ledger. It carries globals, functions, classes, time budget and, for a mid-feed snapshot, the paused call stack — but it does not authenticate effects or establish that an external operation completed or did not. The reference is explicit: 'Neither restored memory nor a timeout establishes that no effect happened' (be447cba9594), and 'A timeout alone never proves that no effect occurred' (5492db3e2b23). Restoring a snapshot is not approval, authentication or a durable effect ledger (ad2668b16ffb).",
